==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Marinmizu''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mizuririn''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Mizunade''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Mizli is best suited to provide support against short-ranged Aliens, such as [[Nimoy Bore]]. Although unreliable, several can easily steamroll [[Into the Future]] if Alien pushers are present, as well as providing decent help against certain Starred Aliens, such as [[Star Peng]], a melee enemy notorious for its extreme pushing power. Its lack of survivability and lengthy recharge time prevent it from being very effective, though, not to mention how it's not useful against ranged threats like [[Calamary]] and [[Alpacky]].

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Capable of Barrier-Breaking and being immune to Warp, Marinmizu is built for fending off strong Starred Aliens, this time with more range and reliability, which allows it to perform better than its Normal Form almost all the time. Some stages that grant a lot of time for stacking can be exceptions. However, due to the extreme prevalence of Alien backliners, Marinmizu's knockback effect can inadvertently destroy your other units by pushing frontline threats away, causing them to walk into the line of fire. This does have, to a degree, some synergy with Snipers, but said Snipers can also come under attack as a result.

For this reason, it tends to pair very badly with [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Solar Cat]], as well as most Ubers and slow-attacking Cats in general. However, it works quite well with pushers or long-ranged Cats, especially if these Cats have some [[Hitbox#Subdivisions|piercing range]] too. They can also be used quite efficiently to re-gain ground on enemy armies that are mostly Alien, even against the likes of [[Cli-One]]. Just make sure to use this time to defend and build up money, then resume the attack once Marinmizu dies and the enemies start advancing again.

The topic described above, known as Mizli syndrome, has very mixed opinions from people. As stated earlier, Aliens have a lot of backliners, however a lot of them don't actually pose a threat if left out in the open. Some examples of helpless backliners include [[Ribbo]], [[Le'Solar]], [[Corporal Weyland]], and many others. In short, it is up to the user whether or not Mizli is useful. If you really struggle with it, simply don't bring Mizli on a stage with backliners.

==='''True Form'''===
Mizuririn only gains health and damage. This barely makes a difference in how it performs against Aliens, aside from the fact that it can push back long ranged enemies more effectively due to better health. It also makes Mizuririn a better generalist, basically giving it a better chance of being useful in stages that have more than just Aliens. Additionally, its stats make it viable as a pure generalist in some stages where money would be too tight for more powerful but expensive units, though this is rare.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Mizunade's most notable improvements are in the form of multiple stat increases that allow it to function as a better specialist support and generalist backliner. Not only that, the addition of two new abilities are even bigger game-changers overall.

Level 2 [[Surge Attack#Mini-Surge|Mini-Surges]] grant it forward pierce, which attenuates its most heavily criticized issue of knocking frontline pushers into the range of backline supports. In addition, it brings Mizunade's damage per attack cycle up to 15,500, which is impressive and allows it to function in a wider variety of roles similarly to [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-03 Cloud Emperor]]. However, with the spawn radius being as broad as it is, the practicality of this ability can be dubious on occasion. Treat it as a bonus, and don't expect it to save the day when the going gets rough.

Finally, [[Sage Slayer]] lacks much practical application outside of the stat bonuses provided. While [[Techn-Old Hyena]] may seem like a good target for Mizunade, his Counter-Surge ability gives way to the possibility of Counter-Mini-Surges Warping away multiple levels of defense, forcing Mizunade to move forth and win your war all by its lonesome. It is, however, very decent against [[Sage of Selection Darvin]], being a well-rounded support/DPS/tank for his stage, and lasting for eons! Sage Slayer also makes Mizunade a phenomenal anti-Sage DPS against the enemies it outranges, such as [[Doctor K.O.]], [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], and [[Oldstrich]].

So while simple, this Ultra Form is very powerful! Transforming Mizunade into an above-average carry that fits into any lineup. And if you do still worry about Mizli Syndrome, backliner-heavy stages are getting less common as the current meta is more focused on rushing and pure power.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Health Buff''' and '''Attack Buff''' CAN make Mizuririn quite good as a general attacker, if there is also help from Catseyes. However, these are just too expensive to be worth the trouble when better attackers and places to spend NP exist.

Due to its tendency to push into longer-ranged units, the '''Survive''' ability turns out to be inconsequential in most cases and should be avoided too. It could sometimes lead to one more hit, though this is not always a guarantee. More aggressive Aliens will do everything in their power to keep Mizuririn from really taking advantage of this Talent, and it has no real chance in tougher non-Alien stages.

Similarly, although '''Slow''' is a straight improvement, only a second more at most will, once again, prove inconsequential in most cases. Furthermore, Slow ends up making the unit worse, as frontliners may be stuck for a split second, which may well be enough for your units to step too far ahead.

Lastly, '''Slow Resist''' is going to come into play so rarely to be worth even less than any other Talent, since very few Aliens inflict slow, and it doesn't ever negate this effect entirely. It can outrange [[Imperator Sael]] already, and it isn't an ideal option for [[Croakley]] stages, as well as against [[Queen B]]. It could possibly see use against [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] and [[Super Hyppoh]], those situations are too infrequent to warrant the NP cost, especially considering Super Hyppoh has too much support for this unit to be useful in this first place.

